<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import InspectPayload from './lib/InspectPayload.abide'
import inspectPayload from './lib/InspectPayload.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import SearchPayload from './lib/SearchPayload.abide'
import searchPayload from './lib/SearchPayload.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/tree', '/helpers/highlight', '/headless/virtual-list']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a row per value, told apart by its pointer, with the root open'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a click picks a row, and the row picked is inspected'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: ['test("a row\'s toggle opens and shuts it, and picks nothing"'],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a search shows its matches and what holds them, opened and marked'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a row shut during a search stays shut until the search changes'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/ops/lib/WebhookPayload.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a matching row keeps everything it holds'"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Inspect a webhook payload">
        <p>Hand <code>jsonInspector</code> a JSON value and it is a row per value, each told apart
            by its JSON Pointer. The rows are flat: render <code>rows</code> as one list, spread
            <code>row(row).item</code> on each, and indent by <code>row.level</code>. The keys are
            <code>tree</code>'s, so Right opens an object, Left closes it, and a click or Enter picks
            the row <code>inspected</code> answers. A click opens nothing, so give each object
            and array a button that calls <code>row(row).toggle</code>.</p>
        <Example code={inspectPayload}><InspectPayload /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Search keys and values">
        <p>Spread <code>search</code> on an input. While it holds text, only the rows that match
            show, with the rows holding them opened. <code>keyRuns</code> and
            <code>valueRuns</code> mark what was found. Clear the search and the tree is as you left
            it.</p>
        <Example code={searchPayload}><SearchPayload /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
